From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafael Guariento <rafaelguariento@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:01:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: arm_scmi: perf: Ignore sustained frequency below
 the lowest OPP

On Snapdragon X1P-64-100 laptops the firmware reports a sustained
frequency of 0 kHz for some performance domains. Every OPP is then
above the sustained frequency and gets marked as turbo, which leaves
cpufreq with no usable frequency and drops the policy.

Ignore a sustained frequency that is below the domain's lowest OPP.
Genuine boost OPPs on parts whose firmware reports a sensible sustained
frequency are unaffected.

Observed on a Dell Inspiron 14 Plus 7441 (X1P-64-100):

  cpu cpu4: [1][NCC1]: sustained freq 0 kHz below lowest OPP, not marking turbo OPPs
  cpu cpu7: [2][NCC2]: sustained freq 0 kHz below lowest OPP, not marking turbo OPPs

Origin: rafaelguariento, https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/discussions/12441
        (discussioncomment-18568484)
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

---
 drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c
index 4583d02be..8e7a1aaa3 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c
@@ -865,14 +865,33 @@ static int scmi_dvfs_device_opps_add(const struct scmi_protocol_handle *ph,
 				     struct device *dev, u32 domain)
 {
 	int idx, ret;
-	unsigned long freq;
+	unsigned long freq, min_freq = ULONG_MAX;
 	struct dev_pm_opp_data data = {};
 	struct perf_dom_info *dom;
+	bool sustained_valid;
 
 	dom = scmi_perf_domain_lookup(ph, domain);
 	if (IS_ERR(dom))
 		return PTR_ERR(dom);
 
+	for (idx = 0; idx < dom->opp_count; idx++) {
+		if (!dom->level_indexing_mode)
+			freq = dom->opp[idx].perf * dom->mult_factor;
+		else
+			freq = dom->opp[idx].indicative_freq * dom->mult_factor;
+		min_freq = min(min_freq, freq);
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Some firmware reports a sustained frequency below the lowest OPP
+	 * (e.g. zero) for some domains. Treating every OPP as turbo then
+	 * leaves cpufreq with no usable frequency, so the policy is dropped.
+	 */
+	sustained_valid = dom->sustained_freq_khz * 1000UL >= min_freq;
+	if (!sustained_valid)
+		dev_info(dev, "[%d][%s]: sustained freq %u kHz below lowest OPP, not marking turbo OPPs\n",
+			 domain, dom->info.name, dom->sustained_freq_khz);
+
 	for (idx = 0; idx < dom->opp_count; idx++) {
 		if (!dom->level_indexing_mode)
 			freq = dom->opp[idx].perf * dom->mult_factor;
@@ -880,7 +899,8 @@ static int scmi_dvfs_device_opps_add(const struct scmi_protocol_handle *ph,
 			freq = dom->opp[idx].indicative_freq * dom->mult_factor;
 
 		/* All OPPs above the sustained frequency are treated as turbo */
-		data.turbo = freq > dom->sustained_freq_khz * 1000UL;
+		data.turbo = sustained_valid &&
+			     freq > dom->sustained_freq_khz * 1000UL;
 
 		data.level = dom->opp[idx].perf;
 		data.freq = freq;
